※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4471

※ The loop stands where a statement stands, so what it comes to is read by
※ nothing and a value handed over here would be worked out and thrown away.  A
※ loop whose value is wanted is written where one is wanted.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    while §counting true:
        break §counting 5u8
    0u6
